 `npm test` runs the existing gateway transport tests and public CLI subprocess
 tests using a local fake proxy; no live gateway, OCR or extraction is called.
+
+## Local help and invocation errors
+
+All help is English and bundled into the standalone executable. No checkout,
+network, SSO session, or external documentation reader is needed:
+
+```bash
+skylark --help
+skylark listing -h
+skylark export --help
+skylark listing --help --full
+skylark export -h --full
+skylark --version
+```
+
+Normal command help includes a first invocation, input type/path bases, environment
+prerequisites, output/write scope, exit codes, and next actions. Add `--full` to a
+help request for the complete schemas, default gateway/environment behavior, and
+boundary rules. `--full` alone is a usage error. `--version` is root-only.
+
+Unknown commands/options, missing arguments/values, and wrong-command options
+return 64 with a concrete stderr diagnostic and the relevant `--help` hint.
+Malformed/unreadable request JSON is a command failure (1); source failures can
+produce a structured partial export report (2). The business meanings of these
+codes are unchanged.
+
+All CLI paths, including export request document paths, resolve from the current
+working directory. A request file does not change the base directory. Select
+distinct request, report, and per-document output paths: path collisions and
+duplicate request targets are not rejected. Repeated invocations fetch remote
+sources again and atomically replace successful local outputs; there is no CLI
+resume or reusable result cache. Inspect the report before choosing a retry.
+
+`npm test` also exercises all root/listing/export short, long, and full-help
+routes, version and usage diagnostics from subprocesses with unavailable gateway
+settings. The test uses a poison proxy and checks isolated HOME/cwd for writes.
